===== ENGINEERING DEBT ACCEPTED =====
1. Schema drift:
Active schema/package wording must be aligned so Architect returns PlanGraph and
Executor/DAG returns ResultProposal. Old or confusing wording such as
must_return_result_proposals_only in Architect-facing instructions must be fixed
in a later schema alignment layer.

2. Runtime validation vs JSON Schema contracts:
Post V&V currently demonstrates deterministic runtime boundary checks, but this
is not yet full nested JSON Schema validation for every artifact. A later Runtime
JSON Schema Validation Hardening layer is required.

3. Evidence kind mismatch:
EvidenceItem.kind / artifact type vocabulary must be aligned with runtime
artifacts such as connector observations, evidence candidates, child boundary
snapshots, audit events, and fractal/DAG executor traces. A later schema
alignment layer must resolve this.

4. Demo B is applied proof, not engine:
Demo B proves document/evidence workflow expressed under Root authority. It does
not prove a real document processing engine.

